.TH CIPHERS 1 "2026-05-23" "hako" "hako utilities"
.SH NAME
ciphers \- probe TLS 1.3 cipher suite support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ciphers
.I host[:port]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ciphers
opens a separate TLS 1.3 handshake for each of the three standard cipher
suites and reports whether the server accepted each one.
.PP
The three suites probed are:
.RS
.TP
.B TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
.TP
.B TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
.TP
.B TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256
.RE
.PP
Each suite is attempted independently so partial support is detected correctly.
The default port is
.BR 443 .
.PP
The
.I host
argument also accepts an
.B https://
or
.B tls://
URL; the path component is ignored.
.SH OUTPUT
One line per cipher suite, padded to a fixed width, followed by
.B ok
or
.BR no :
.PP
.nf
TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256       ok
TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384       ok
TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 ok
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "ciphers example.com"
Probe cipher suite support at
.BR example.com:443 .
.TP
.B "ciphers example.com:8443"
Probe cipher suite support at
.BR example.com:8443 .
.TP
.B "ciphers https://example.com"
Same as the first example; the URL form is accepted for convenience.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All three suites were probed successfully (individual
.B no
results are not errors).
.TP
.B 1
Wrong arguments or a network-level failure that prevented any probe from
completing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tlscheck (1),
.BR fetch (1),
.BR hako (1)
